  <prompt>Establish empirically whether a delegated Microsoft Graph token carrying FileStorageContainerType.Manage.All can be obtained via the per-customer owning app against the Spaarke Dev tenant. This is a SPIKE: produce evidence and a documented token-acquisition shape, not production code. Two verified defects mean the existing path cannot work as written — determine whether they are fixable within the owning-app model.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in MSAL confidential clients, the OAuth 2.0 On-Behalf-Of flow, Entra app registrations, token audiences, and Microsoft Graph SPE permissions. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A documented, evidenced answer to: can the per-customer owning app obtain a Graph-audienced delegated token for containerTypes? Either a working token-acquisition shape recorded for task 011 to implement, or an evidenced determination that the shape is unworkable — which reopens the §6.5 ADR gate.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec §3.1, ADR Tensions, and Unresolved Question 1 — the project's highest-risk unknown. GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes does not support application permissions at all, so Container Types cannot work under the current app-only posture regardless of credentials. The §6.5 gate is resolved as path C (comply under ADR-028 E-1), because ADR-028 A4 exempts per-customer owning apps from the no-client-secret rule and spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI explicitly scopes SpeAdminTokenProvider/SpeAdminGraphService out of its migration (its design.md:149).

BUT two verified defects mean the existing owning-app OBO path cannot currently succeed:
(1) SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs:142 requests scope api://{OwningAppId}/.default — an owning-app audience — while the resulting token is handed to a Graph client pointed at graph.microsoft.com (SpeAdminGraphService.cs:4212). Graph rejects on audience. Corroborated independently by projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md:22.
(2) SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs:306 builds the confidential client as Create(config.OwningAppId), but MSAL OBO requires the incoming user assertion to be audienced to that same client — while the SPE Admin code page authenticates against the BFF (api://{bff-client-id}/SDAP.Access).

Together these indicate the SPE-084 multi-app OBO path has likely NEVER executed successfully, consistent with spec §1's finding that no test makes a real Graph call.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/SpeAdmin/SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeAdminGraphService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/design.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2/notes/obo-spike-findings.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No task prerequisites. Requires the Spaarke Dev tenant and its owning-app registration.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this task is a SPIKE. Produce evidence and a documented shape. Do NOT ship the production implementation — that is task 011.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the credential for the delegated exchange. Stay on the PER-CUSTOMER OWNING APP identity (exception E-1). MUST NOT route the exchange through the BFF app registration — that lands in Amendment A4 territory (MI-FIC or KV certificate required, never a client secret), trips E-3's "does not license expansion" clause, and contradicts auth-v4's scoping decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: any NEW confidential client. MUST NOT add a new .WithClientSecret site for a client authenticating as the BFF identity. The existing owning-app secret usage is covered by E-1 and is not being expanded by this spike.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: secrets. Do NOT write any secret VALUE, token, or assertion into notes, logs, or the repo. Record shapes, audiences, scopes, claim names, and error codes only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: tenant safety. Read-only Graph calls only. This spike MUST NOT create, modify, or delete a container type.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>OBO flow, token audiences, SPE container-type permissions</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
