    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="obo-flow" location=".claude/patterns/auth/obo-flow.md">Canonical OBO exchange shape and its audience requirements.</pattern>
      <pattern name="oauth-scopes" location=".claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md">Scope construction — .default vs individual scopes.</pattern>
      <pattern name="token-caching" location=".claude/patterns/auth/token-caching.md">Per-(config + user) cache keying and TTL.</pattern>
      <pattern name="graph-endpoints-catalog" location=".claude/patterns/auth/graph-endpoints-catalog.md">Which Graph endpoints support delegated vs application permissions.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Load ADR-028 (all amendments, especially A4 + exceptions E-1/E-3), spec ADR Tensions, and the two defect sites.</step>
    <step order="1">Confirm defect (1) by reading SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs:142 and SpeAdminGraphService.cs:4212. Record the actual scope requested and the actual Graph base URL used.</step>
    <step order="2">Confirm defect (2) by reading SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs:306 and determining the audience of the token the SPE Admin code page actually sends to the BFF.</step>
    <step order="3">Determine which app registration can legitimately perform the OBO exchange given the incoming assertion's audience. Document the constraint precisely — this is the crux.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify the Spaarke Dev owning app's delegated permission state: is FileStorageContainerType.Manage.All granted and admin-consented? Record the finding (do NOT grant it from this task).</step>
    <step order="5">Attempt to obtain a Graph-audienced delegated token via the owning app. Try the corrected scope (https://graph.microsoft.com/.default) and record the exact result — success, or the precise MSAL/Entra error code.</step>
    <step order="6">If a token is obtained: call GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes (v1.0) with it and record the HTTP status and payload shape.</step>
    <step order="7">Also verify the §4.2b claim empirically: does container-type LIST work for a non-admin owning-tenant user (ownership-filtered), and does CREATE genuinely need no admin role? The Graph reference page and the conceptual doc contradict each other — record which is correct.</step>
    <step order="8">Write projects/sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2/notes/obo-spike-findings.md: the working shape (if found), the exact client/audience/scope triple, the permission prerequisites, and any residual risk. No secret values.</step>
    <step order="9">Decide the outcome: WORKABLE (hand the shape to task 011) or UNWORKABLE (fire the escalation trigger and reopen the §6.5 gate).</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 010 status to ✅ and record the outcome verdict beside it.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owning-app shape CANNOT obtain a Graph-audienced delegated token, STOP. Do NOT fall back to the BFF app registration on your own initiative. Re-run the CLAUDE.md §6.5 ADR Conflict block with the new evidence — the fallback lands in ADR-028 A4 territory and requires coordination with spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI plus a named human path A/B decision. Write BLOCKED.md and stop.</trigger>
    <trigger>If making the owning-app shape work would require the SPE Admin code page to acquire a second, owning-app-audienced token (a client-side auth change), STOP and escalate — that is a change to the client auth contract under ADR-028 and is a scope decision, not a task-level choice.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Spaarke Dev owning app lacks the required delegated permission or consent, STOP and escalate with the exact permission named. Granting Entra permissions is an operator action, not a task action.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SpeAdminTokenProvider.cs already implements an OBO exchange with per-(configId + sha256(userToken)) caching (SpeAdminGraphService.cs:448-498). Grep confirms no second OBO implementation exists for SpeAdmin.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — the intent is to REPAIR the existing provider, not add a parallel path. This spike determines whether repair is possible within the owning-app model before any code is written.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Container Types returns an error permanently: GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes does not support application permissions at all, so no credential value fixes it. Without this spike, task 011 would be built on an assumption that two verified defects contradict.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/run a scratch verification harness</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
