  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Both defects are confirmed or refuted against the code, with file:line evidence recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The question "which app registration can perform the OBO exchange given the incoming assertion's audience" is answered precisely and recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the corrected scope, when a token acquisition is attempted via the owning app, then either a Graph-audienced token is obtained (recorded with its audience claim) or the exact MSAL/Entra error code is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If a token was obtained, GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes (v1.0) returns 200 and the payload shape is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The §4.2b contradiction (reference page vs conceptual doc on whether create needs an admin role) is resolved empirically and recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/obo-spike-findings.md contains no secret value, token, or assertion — only shapes, audiences, scopes, claim names, and error codes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no container type was created, modified, or deleted during the spike.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A WORKABLE or UNWORKABLE verdict is recorded. If UNWORKABLE, BLOCKED.md exists and the §6.5 gate is flagged for re-run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-B01. THE highest-risk task in the project (spec Unresolved Question 1). Tasks 011 and 012 depend on its outcome; task 004 may hand off to it. Parallel-safe: produces notes only, no source modification — runs alongside task 004 in Wave 2.

COMPLETED 2026-08-21 — VERDICT: **UNWORKABLE**. Full evidence in notes/obo-spike-findings.md; escalation in BLOCKED.md.

Escalation triggers 1 and 2 BOTH FIRED. Trigger 3 did NOT (permissions are already granted).

THE PREMISE WAS FALSE. sprk_owningappid = 170c98e1 = SDAP-PCF-CLIENT — the SPA client the code page already signs in as. There is NO per-customer owning app in this environment, so ADR-028 E-1 ("per-customer owning apps, which are other applications identities") does not describe the situation. The §6.5 gate resolved as path C on that premise and must be RE-RUN.

Defect 1 CONFIRMED and worse than described: api://{owningAppId}/.default returns AADSTS500011 "resource principal not found" — SDAP-PCF-CLIENT has NO identifierUris and NO exposed scopes, so the scope can never resolve. Not a wrong audience; an impossible one.

Defect 2 CONFIRMED and structurally unfixable: OBO requires the exchanging confidential client to BE the assertion audience. Assertion aud = 1e40baad (BFF); code builds Create(170c98e1). Cannot be fixed by configuration because 170c98e1 can never be an audience.

Permissions are NOT the problem: FileStorageContainerType.Manage.All is delegated + admin-consented on BOTH service principals.

Spec §3.1 CONFIRMED: app-only GET /storage/fileStorage/containerTypes returns 403 accessDenied on v1.0 AND beta.

STEP 7 NOT RESOLVED — the §4.2b list-vs-create admin-role contradiction needs a delegated token, obtainable only via the broken OBO path, an interactive sign-in, or a forbidden create. Carried to task 011, which will hold a working token. Recorded honestly rather than inferred from the contradicting docs.

DO NOT switch Create(OwningAppId) -> Create(BffAppId). That is exactly what trigger 1 forbids: ADR-028 A4 territory, a NEW site under E-3, and it contradicts spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI design.md:149. A human picks path A/B/C in BLOCKED.md.

Read-only throughout — no container type created, modified, or deleted. No secret value written anywhere.
</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
